From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000113 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <colum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:29:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dsv41): TF_SPILL_STRIDE=N keeps every Nth old turn manifest at a trim
 (unset: as before)

core/spill's trimPath deletes every turn manifest on a conversation's active path past the newest
TF_SPILL_TURNS at each publish: the blocks survive (the newer point's manifest names them) but the
older cuts become unresumable, so a regenerate, rewind or branch back past the window re-encodes the
whole middle (docs/prefix-cache-hitrate-review.md finding 5).

With TF_SPILL_STRIDE=N (u32, N >= 1) every Nth turn past the window stays as well, at most
store.stride_kept_max (64) extra manifests per path so the point index stays bounded: kept cuts are
turns t, t-N, t-2N, ... anchored in each point's in-memory turn depth from the branch root (the
root at depth 1, so every depth stays on the stride's grid), so they survive later publishes; a
reopen takes every surviving manifest as one stride and strides on from there. Eviction (victims,
quota, floor) is unchanged and still governs disk pressure; the stride only
changes what trimPath deletes at publish.

TF_SPILL_STRIDE is plumbed exactly like TF_SPILL_TURNS: server/cli.zig's spill_env list and spill()
parse, engine_api's api.Spill, spillSettings into spill_tier.Settings, and Settings.follower's
environment on the follower ranks (start.sh passes TF_SPILL_* to both). Like turns today it is
per-rank and compared nowhere (not in the fingerprint's features nor storeCompat); a rank whose trim
kept a point another rank dropped is handled by the existing rank_wire presence flow.

Unset/0: trimPath removes exactly the manifests it removed before, and every new setting stays inert;
no manifest format and no kernel shape changes.

Tests: zig build test and zig/tests/server/zig_test.sh pass; core/spill store checks "stride" (kept
set is t, t-N, t-2N... plus the newest turns, N=2 and N=3), "stride off" (unset keeps exactly the
newest 4), "stride cap" (64 extras past the window, the oldest gone) and "stride restart" (the
extras survive a reopen and the next publish's trim); cli's spill test and the follower-settings
test cover the two env reads. Not run on a pair.
---
diff --git a/zig/src/core/engine_api.zig b/zig/src/core/engine_api.zig
